From d2e130f22987b555de731918e3979510ce5cd36e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Medium1992 <Medium1992@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 01:50:26 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 18/19] XHTTP: Harden the HTTP/2 flow governor against hostile
 and unusual peers

- Pass malformed control frames on unchanged: SETTINGS or PING off stream 0,
  SETTINGS with any invalid value, and every frame inside a HEADERS or
  PUSH_PROMISE header block. Recognise the ACK of every outstanding PING.
- End the connection when a write of rewritten frames fails, so no frame
  follows a torn one.
- Follow SETTINGS_INITIAL_WINDOW_SIZE changes on open streams: credit them
  after a raise, show a lowered value low enough for credit already handed
  on, and give the connection up when no value is.
- Queue upload credit per stream, dropped with the stream; give up a
  connection that makes the governor track more than 4096 streams.
- Govern the upload connection window: what the streams whose readers take
  data may hold, plus Go's 1 MiB for the rest.
- Grant no upload credit to a request that has already ended, as the stock
  server, and send the guard PING only while a stream waits for credit.
